The registry-first sample tests/registry/uy.jsonl contains addresses, postcodes and coordinates
from Direcciones Geográficas del Uruguay, published by the Infraestructura de Datos Espaciales
(IDE Uruguay) on information of the Correo Uruguayo, on the Catálogo de Datos Abiertos
(https://catalogodatos.gub.uy/dataset/ide-direcciones-geograficas-del-uruguay): the address
points of the 19 departments ("Direcciones - ARTIGAS" to "Direcciones - TREINTA Y TRES"), data
of 2026-10-01, downloaded on 2026-10-30. Provider: Infraestructura de Datos Espaciales (IDE
Uruguay), Correo Uruguayo and AGESIC.
Used under the "Licencia de Datos Abiertos – Uruguay", version 0.1
(https://www.gub.uy/agencia-gobierno-electronico-sociedad-informacion-conocimiento/sites/agencia-gobierno-electronico-sociedad-informacion-conocimiento/files/documentos/publicaciones/licencia_de_datos_abiertos_0.pdf).
Changes: the department files were converted from Windows-1252 to UTF-8, joined
(tests/registry/dgu-csv.sql) and a sample drawn; the door number and letter were written
together and the query forms constructed from the register's fields, not by the IDE or the
Correo Uruguayo, which have not approved this sample. Per-case file checksums and retrieval
dates are recorded in the corpus; docs/evaluation/registry/uy.md records the upstream checksums.
